STRATA Pseudocode

```text
PASSAGE enters the chamber.

LOCK the witness:
    Do not silently substitute a different manuscript, edition, or language tradition.

CUT the passage into tokens without destroying punctuation or cantillation/diacritics.

FOR each token:
    ASK what form is physically present.
    ASK what lemma(s) can generate it.
    ASK what morphology constrains it.
    ASK what senses are attested in the relevant period.
    ASK what older/neighboring senses remain audible.
    ASK what the same author/corpus does with the form elsewhere.
    STORE all answers with provenance.

BUILD every materially plausible syntax tree.
DO NOT choose yet.

LISTEN:
    repetitions
    alliteration
    assonance
    rhyme
    rhythm
    root echo
    near-homophone
    word-order emphasis

COMPARE witnesses.
KEEP textual variation separate from interpretive variation.

MAKE a Reading Lattice:
    branches are alternatives;
    evidence prunes branches;
    uncertainty stays visible.

GENERATE English candidates only after the lattice exists.

FOR each candidate:
    measure what survived;
    measure what vanished;
    rescue high-value loss into notes.

OUTPUT four synchronized interfaces:
    FLUENT  = experience the text
    GLASS   = see through English toward the source
    X-RAY   = inspect linguistic machinery
    STRATA  = see history, ambiguity, art, variants, and uncertainty

THE READER may compress.
THE ENGINE may not silently erase.
```